  "label": "User projected onto the textual material expressing a conditional statement about friendship",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'if you're not grilling at my grave site we were never really friends' because the text uses the second-person pronoun 'you' and the first-person possessive 'my', directly addressing the viewer as the person who must fulfill the condition to be considered a true friend. This creates an implicit 'you' as the projected user, who is being judged by the meme's logic.",
